before:
The transform is visually zero, but establishes a fixed containing block. The badge now sits 12px from the host’s padding edge. translateX(0px) is a CSS transform function: its one length argument is horizontal displacement; zero moves nothing.
```css
.demo { writing-mode: horizontal-tb; direction: ltr; }
.host { height: 100px; } .badge { position: fixed; top: 10px; left: 12px; width: 60px; height: 20px; background: navy; color: white; } .host { transform: translateX(0px); position: relative; margin-left: 30px; }
```

after:
This badge sits 10 pixels below the top and 12 pixels from the left.
```css
.badge {
  position: fixed;
  top: 10px;
  left: 12px;
}
```
